<title>UK: British Telecom up on squeeze.</title>
<headline>British Telecom up on squeeze.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Telecommunications were squeezed higher on Monday amid arbitrage-linked trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0940 GMT, the shares were up 9-1/2p to 378p, the highest level since mid-September.</p>
<p>Dealers said the shares have fluctuated on arbitrage-related dealings against shares in MCI Communications Corp since the merger between the two companies was announced earlier this month.</p>
<p>Shares in MCI on Friday ended $1-1/8 higher at $29-3/4.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
